.TH bhtune-history-prune 1  "bhtune-history-prune "
.SH NAME
bhtune\-history\-prune \- Delete runs older than the configured retention policy (`history\-retention`), without waiting for the next automatic startup sweep
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-history\-prune\fR [\fB\-\-older\-than\-days\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete runs older than the configured retention policy (`history\-retention`), without waiting for the next automatic startup sweep
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-older\-than\-days\fR \fI<OLDER_THAN_DAYS>\fR
Delete runs older than this many days, overriding the configured `retention_days` policy for this invocation only. Required if no retention policy is configured at all (`\-\-retention\-days` / `BHTUNE_RETENTION_DAYS` / the config file\*(Aqs `retention_days` key) \-\- there is no default "prune everything older than X" to fall back to
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report how many runs would be deleted, and as of what cutoff, without deleting anything
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
How to print the prune outcome
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Human\-readable text (default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Pretty\-printed JSON. This is the external contract for scripted/scheduled consumers, so its shape must not change silently once shipped
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
